# --- Portal -> ERP connection ------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only. The browser never talks to Frappe directly: every call goes
# through a Next.js route handler that holds the ERP `sid` in an HttpOnly cookie
# on this origin. Do NOT prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ - that would publish it.
#
# The hostname must be the site that actually answers /api/method/ping with 200.
# Two hostnames can point at the same server while only one is a working site;
# verify before reporting a login failure:
#
#     npm run check:erp
#
# Example: https://erp.example.com
FRAPPE_BASE_URL=

# --- Diagnostics --------------------------------------------------------------
# Portal-side request logging, on the Next.js *server* output (never the browser
# console). Every failed call prints the host, the HTTP status and the ERP's own
# exception type, e.g.
#   [frappe] shikkha_os.api.v1.auth.login -> erp.example.com failed: host=...
#   [auth]   login rejected for someone@example.com: code=upstream_error status=502
# Set to 0 to silence it (the ERP keeps writing its own Error Log either way).
FRAPPE_DEBUG_LOG=1
